{"id": "EUVD-2026-76381", "enisaUuid": "ba979c34-4805-3684-b7be-25a70006c619", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npower: supply: bq24257: fix use-after-free on remove\n\nThe STAT-pin interrupt is devm-managed, so it stays armed until the devm\ncleanup that runs after remove() returns. remove() cancels\nbq->iilimit_setup_work while the threaded handler can still fire; that\nhandler reschedules the work and dereferences bq, so the work runs\nagainst freed memory once devm frees bq.\n\nMake the delayed work device-managed with devm_delayed_work_autocancel(),\nregistered before the interrupt request. The devm cleanup then releases\nthe interrupt first, so the handler can no longer reschedule the work,\nand cancels the work before bq is freed. The explicit\ncancel_delayed_work_sync() in remove() is no longer needed and is dropped.\n\nFound by static analysis.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:47:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d77fd7dd9a3ad57f7655c5264b503b85adbb7b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a279e64c907f5638bb34cb8e2c9285798cf5f690", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6d2eb93975c07b0169a3287efc1ae3b60cf52d8e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/861ec73ce86e2ca18082cc7be4f140a5bbdf1428", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f495808cdd6d9576965787cf6d9737d0b0e86b73", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/47ccbad210f48721c30d69d65b83dc9fff919ca9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d34c9d660c3d0931d2cc749c46c47cf31f96e48"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pg63-6v2p-p54j", "CVE-2026-89475"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "22a1be28-e8b2-3fc6-b1d7-f684eae0f8d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "2ba7e16e-2a40-32ed-b824-60a58b747335", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "2e2199ca-bb40-38ba-b55d-dd8271